{{/*
	Forgejo's own partial, kept identical except for the theme link's version. Forgejo lets browsers cache theme
	files for hours and versions this link with its own release only, so an updated theme kept rendering with the
	previous stylesheet. The build appends the theme's content version after AssetVersion.

	The script marks pages opened in a project board's side panel, before they paint, so the panel shows the issue
	without the site navigation, and names the issue's repository for organization and user projects. The frame name
	survives navigation inside the panel.

	No render-blocking expect link: holding the first paint until the whole page was parsed left large pages, such as
	a big pull request's files, blank for over half a second longer.
*/}}
<script>if (window.name.startsWith("github-project-panel") && window.parent !== window) document.documentElement.classList.add("github-embedded", ...(window.name.endsWith("-owner") ? ["github-embedded-owner"] : []));</script>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{AssetUrlPrefix}}/css/index.css?v={{AssetVersion}}">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{AssetUrlPrefix}}/css/theme-{{ThemeName .SignedUser | PathEscape}}.css?v={{AssetVersion}}">
